Question: A certain shopping mall is holding a promotional event where customers can participate in a lottery for every 300 yuan spent. Each customer can draw three times, and each draw costs 1 yuan. If a customer draws twice and does not draw a card, they need to spend another 300 yuan to draw again. If they draw a card this time, they win a prize; otherwise, they need to spend another 300 yuan and draw again, continuing this process until they draw a card to win a prize. It is known that the probability of winning a prize each time is $\frac{1}{4}$, and the random variable $\xi$ represents the amount of money that needs to be spent to draw a winning card.


Find the probability distribution of the random variable $\xi$.

Solution: Since the random variable $\xi$ represents the amount of money that needs to be spent to draw a winning card, $\xi$ can take values of 300 yuan, 600 yuan, 900 yuan, 1200 yuan, and 1500 yuan.

$\because $ When the value of event A, "drawing a winning card on the first attempt", is $300;

When the value of event B, "drawing a losing card on the first attempt and a winning card on the second attempt", is 600;

When the value of event C, "drawing losing cards on the first two attempts and a winning card on the third attempt", is 900;

When the value of event D, "drawing losing cards on the first three attempts and a winning card on the fourth attempt", is 1200;

When the value of event E, "drawing losing cards on the first four attempts and a winning card on the fifth attempt", is 1500;

$\therefore $ The probabilities of events B, C, D, and E are respectively: $P(B) = \frac{1}{4} \times \frac{3}{4} = \frac{3}{16}$, $P(C) = \frac{3}{4} \times \frac{3}{4} \times \frac{1}{4} = \frac{9}{64}$, $P(D) = \frac{3}{4} \times \frac{3}{4} \times \frac{3}{4} \times \frac{1}{4} = \frac{27}{256}$, $P(E) = \frac{3}{4} \times \frac{3}{4} \times \frac{3}{4} \times \frac{3}{4} \times \frac{1}{4} = \frac{81}{1024}$.

$\therefore $ The probability of the random variable $\xi$ is as follows:

$$
\begin{array}{c|ccccc}
\xi & 300 & 600 & 900 & 1200 & 1500 \\
\hline
P & \frac{1}{4} & \frac{3}{16} & \frac{9}{64} & \frac{27}{256} & \frac{81}{1024} \\
\end{array}
$$

Answer:  
The probability distribution of the random variable $\xi$ is:  
